WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.415 --> 00:00:02.994
- The guy bought $117

00:00:02.994 --> 00:00:05.294
case of Pinot Grigio.

00:00:05.294 --> 00:00:07.739
Right, so $10 a bottle 
Pinot Grigio.

00:00:07.739 --> 00:00:10.558
I go in his Twitter account
on this flight and all

00:00:10.558 --> 00:00:12.693
he's tweeting about is following:

00:00:12.693 --> 00:00:16.362
"Jay Cutler, I love you." 
"Jay Cutler, you're the best."

00:00:16.362 --> 00:00:17.869
"Jay Cutler, I'm mad at you."

00:00:17.869 --> 00:00:21.211
For those who don't know 
Jay Cutler is and was at the

00:00:21.211 --> 00:00:23.756
time the quarterback 
for the Chicago Bears.

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:28.454
He's talking about Jay Cutler, 
Jay Cutler so I call my point

00:00:28.454 --> 00:00:29.436
person back at the 
store and I said,

00:00:29.436 --> 00:00:31.955
"Look, I want you to go to eBay

00:00:31.955 --> 00:00:35.618
"and I want you to buy him 
a signed Jay Cutler jersey."

00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:39.016
Which was like $350, 
much more than the 8% profit

00:00:39.016 --> 00:00:42.554
we made on the $111 
case of Pinot Grigio

00:00:42.554 --> 00:00:43.634
"and I want you to send a note

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.637
"in there and say thank 
you for your order.

00:00:45.637 --> 00:00:46.966
"Thanks for shopping Wine Library.'"

00:00:46.966 --> 00:00:51.643
Great, I send it. And then three 
and a half weeks go by and

00:00:51.643 --> 00:00:54.508
nothing happens and I'm like 
this son of a gun is really

00:00:54.508 --> 00:00:57.935
not going to acknowledge
this random kindness.

00:00:57.935 --> 00:01:01.007
We send out some other stuff 
and then out of nowhere,

00:01:01.007 --> 00:01:05.057
actually ironically, 
I'm about to take stage

00:01:05.057 --> 00:01:06.657
at a talk in Las Vegas

00:01:06.657 --> 00:01:09.109
and I get a phone 
call from Kristin.

00:01:09.109 --> 00:01:11.680
She hasn't called me yet.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.183
She works in the 
Thank You Department.

00:01:13.183 --> 00:01:14.281
She doesn't really need me.

00:01:14.281 --> 00:01:16.454
She's only to call me about 
these couple of things we sent

00:01:16.454 --> 00:01:18.746
out and I pick up the phone 
and I go "You got something?"

00:01:18.746 --> 00:01:21.166
She goes "Kind of." 
I go "Go ahead."

00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:24.171
She goes, "I want to read 
you the order we just got."

00:01:24.171 --> 00:01:27.152
She reads off this order and how
many people here are in to wine?

00:01:27.152 --> 00:01:29.098
Great, wow, amazing.

00:01:29.098 --> 00:01:31.898
(laughter)

00:01:31.898 --> 00:01:34.698
This person orders $4,800 worth

00:01:34.698 --> 00:01:38.709
of high end red burgundy. 
Coche Durie, Dugioalic

00:01:38.709 --> 00:01:41.158
like real stuff for the 
real nerds in here.

00:01:41.158 --> 00:01:45.498
And here's what the 
comment box said,

00:01:45.498 --> 00:01:49.724
"Hey, my name is Craig. 
I want you to know you guys

00:01:49.724 --> 00:01:53.293
"sent my friend John

00:01:53.293 --> 00:01:55.903
"a Chicago Bears jersey

00:01:55.903 --> 00:01:58.927
"and he told me the story and

00:01:58.927 --> 00:02:00.592
"that's how I found 
out about you.

00:02:00.592 --> 00:02:02.848
"P.S. You have great prices
on red burgundy.

00:02:02.848 --> 00:02:07.639
" P.S.S. I'm a huge 
Bruce Springsteen fan."

00:02:07.639 --> 00:02:11.615
(laughter)

00:02:11.615 --> 00:02:14.926
The punchline of that story 
is you guys are curating events

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:16.494
and experiences 
that really matter.

00:02:16.494 --> 00:02:19.567
People, today more and 
more as time goes on,

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.861
are sharing more and more 
information about themselves.

00:02:21.861 --> 00:02:25.131
We can cry about privacy but 
everyday we prove with our

00:02:25.131 --> 00:02:26.918
actions that we don't care.

00:02:26.918 --> 00:02:29.386
And really, there's a much more 
fascinating debate over that

00:02:29.386 --> 00:02:31.870
which is that people 
are inherently good.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.406
That mainstream media just 
talks about the small 1% of bad.

00:02:34.406 --> 00:02:35.942
That's why we share our privacy.

00:02:35.942 --> 00:02:38.762
Your ability to know 
a lot more about the

00:02:38.762 --> 00:02:40.808
people that are coming to 
these events is far greater

00:02:40.808 --> 00:02:42.517
than you may believe.

00:02:42.517 --> 00:02:44.905
And that if you actually put in 
the time to understand

00:02:44.905 --> 00:02:47.917
who that is I promise 
you this that if I came

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:50.958
to one of your events as 
a top seller or executive

00:02:50.958 --> 00:02:53.280
and I walked in to my 
hotel room and instead

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.537
of a fruit basket or a 
bottle of wine or a

00:02:55.537 --> 00:02:58.888
nice welcome note that 
there was a New York Jets hat

00:02:58.888 --> 00:03:01.372
that would matter to me 
because that would show

00:03:01.372 --> 00:03:04.281
the thing that matters more 
than anything which is

00:03:04.281 --> 00:03:06.254
intent and effort.

00:03:06.254 --> 00:03:08.254
(light music)

